# M8 walkthrough: secrets, MCP servers, plugins and skills.
# Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension or the JetBrains HTTP client.
# Prerequisites: a default model (m1-providers.http); for plugins' stdio servers, the runner
# (`pnpm stack:up`, or `pnpm dev:runner` next to `pnpm dev`) and `pnpm mcp:up`.

@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:4111
@token = paste-your-admin-token-here
@departmentId = paste-a-department-id
@previewId = paste-a-preview-id
@pluginId = paste-a-plugin-id

### Everything an agent or a department can be given.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/capabilities
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### A secret for a remote MCP server (stored encrypted, never shown again).
PUT {{baseUrl}}/v1/secrets/DOCS_TOKEN
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "value": "paste-the-token", "description": "Docs MCP server" }

### A remote MCP server (Streamable HTTP). Public addresses only, unless "allowPrivateNetwork": true.
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/mcp-servers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "slug": "docs",
  "name": "Docs",
  "url": "https://mcp.example.com/mcp",
  "headers": { "Authorization": { "secret": "DOCS_TOKEN" } }
}

### Preview a plugin from GitHub, pinned to a tag's commit: what it brings, needs and skips.
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/plugins/preview
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "source": { "kind": "github", "repo": "heygen-com/hyperframes", "ref": "v0.8.140" } }

### Install it (stdio servers: "network": "egress" for public sites through the proxy, or "none").
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/plugins
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "previewId": "{{previewId}}", "network": "egress" }

### Its status: installing, installed, or failed (its skills work either way).
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/plugins/{{pluginId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Give a department its skills (all of them, by the plugin's name) and an MCP server's tools.
### Every agent of the department gets them; "requireApproval" makes each call wait for you.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/v1/departments/{{departmentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "skills": ["hyperframes"],
  "mcp": [{ "server": "docs", "tools": ["search"], "requireApproval": false }]
}

### Skills, and one with its files.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/skills
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Uninstall: its skills and servers leave every agent and department, then everything of it goes.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/v1/plugins/{{pluginId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
